# Everything here is read by FreeBSD: shell scripts, rc scripts, Python and
# configuration files. A CRLF checkout on Windows must not turn into a CRLF file
# on the firewall, where /bin/sh would read the carriage return as part of the
# command and an rc script would fail in a way nobody would guess from the error.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary

# What an appliance would carry is the archive of a commit, and nothing it does not read goes into it: the
# documentation, the workflows and the files about the project itself - as in os-blocklists. Nothing here is
# installed yet; a file an appliance starts to read leaves this list in the same change.
docs/ export-ignore
.github/ export-ignore
CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md export-ignore
CONTRIBUTING.md export-ignore
SECURITY.md export-ignore
tools/ export-ignore
/README.md export-ignore
